0101:     """
0102:     Extend every colored segment straight toward the single solid edge bar, with nearer segments covering farther projections.
0103: 
0104:     Input structure
0105:     - The background is the dominant color.
0106:     - Exactly one full grid edge is a solid non-background bar.
0107:     - All other foreground objects are 4-connected, monochrome, one-cell-thick segments parallel to that edge.
0108: 
0109:     Rule
0110:     - Each segment paints the rectangular strip from itself to the cell before the edge bar, perpendicular to the segment.
0111:     - Strips farther from the edge bar are painted first; closer strips overwrite them wherever their rectangular regions overlap.
0112:     - The original edge bar remains unchanged.
0113: 
0114:     Key insight
0115:     - The edge bar acts as the direction cue and occluding wall: every segment casts a same-color projection toward it, and distance to the wall determines visible layering.
